  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Skip to content Astromax Work Services Studio Journal Contact Overview Menu Astromax Close Work Services Studio Journal Contact Overview One colour is enough Most brands we inherit have nine colours and use none of them with conviction. Written by Luc\u00eda Ferrer Published 2 August 2026 Reading time 1 min read Tags Identity Colour Most identities we inherit come with a palette of nine colours, each with a tint scale and a rule about where it may appear. In practice, nobody remembers the rules and every page looks a little different. We now start with one colour and a pair of neutrals. If the brand needs a second colour later, it can earn it. Choosing it We do not start from colour theory. We start from the places the brand will live: a shopfront in winter light, a phone screen at night, a paper bag, a delivery van. A colour that survives all of them is rare, and usually obvious once found. For \u00c6len it was a burnt orange that held up on screen and on cheap uncoated paper. Everything else became black, white and one warm grey. Using it One colour means it has to be used with confidence. Large fields, not thin lines. Whole pages, not buttons. When it appears, it should fe",
